+# DP 3 – DP 5 Curriculum & Capability Development Overview
+
+---
+
+## 1.  Background
+
+| DP | Current CAF rank (in TrueNorth) | Existing QSP code(s) | Comment |
+|----|--------------------------------|----------------------|---------|
+| 1  | **Pte** – Private | **ALJQ** | Defined (Basic occupation) |
+| 2  | **Cpl** – Corporal | **TEMP67, TEMP64, ALRA** | Defined (Journeyman) |
+| 3  | – | – | Placeholder – **Master Corporal (MCpl)** is the logical next rank |
+| 4  | – | – | Placeholder – **Sergeant (Sgt)** |
+| 5  | – | – | Placeholder – **Warrant Officer (WO)** (often called *Sergeant‑Major* in day‑to‑day usage) |
+
+The code in `control-plane/api/app/qsp_paths.py` deliberately leaves DP 3‑5 empty.  The design below shows **what could be added** when official QSPs become available.
+
+---
+
+## 2.  Proposed QSP Definitions
+
+| DP | QSP Code | Rank | Track | Title (displayed in the UI) | Brief Description |
+|----|----------|------|-------|-----------------------------|--------------------|
+| **DP 3** | **MCPL‑001** | **MCpl** (Master Corporal) | `progression` | *Cyber Operator – Technical Specialist (MCpl RQ)* | First NCO rank where the operator becomes a **subject‑matter expert (SME)** for a specific cyber toolset. |
+| **DP 3** | **MCPL‑002** | **MCpl** | `specialty` | *Cyber Analyst – Network Monitoring (MCpl RQ)* | Focuses on continuous network monitoring, packet analysis, and basic intrusion detection. |
+| **DP 4** | **SGT‑001** | **Sgt** (Sergeant) | `progression` | *Cyber Operator – Squad Lead (Sgt RQ)* | SME who now **leads a squad**, planning and executing defensive and offensive cyber missions. |
+| **DP 4** | **SGT‑002** | **Sgt** | `specialty` | *Red Team Lead – Adversary Emulation (Sgt RQ)* | Commands a small **red‑team** cell, designs realistic adversary simulations. |
+| **DP 5** | **WO‑001** | **WO** (Warrant Officer) | `progression` | *Cyber Instructor – Senior Trainer (WO RQ)* | Senior technical instructor, author of curricula, mentor for MCpls and Sgts. |
+| **DP 5** | **WO‑002** | **WO** | `specialty` | *Cyber Operations Architect – Enterprise Defender (WO RQ)* | Designs enterprise‑wide security architectures, integrates multi‑domain defenses. |
+
+*The `track` column mirrors the existing “progression” (core ladder) and “specialty” (parallel streams such as Red Team, Malware) concepts.*
