+## 4.  Mapping to American Standards
+
+| Canadian QSP (DP) | Approx. U.S. MOS / AFSC | NIST CSF Core Functions Covered | NICE Framework **Specialty Areas** |
+|-------------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------|------------------------------------|
+| **MCPL‑001 / MCPL‑002** | **18X** (U.S. Army Cyber Operations Specialist) <br> **1B4X1** (Air Force Cyber Operations) | **Identify**, **Protect**, **Detect** | **Operate & Maintain – Cyber Defense Analyst**, **Analyze – Network Analyst** |
+| **SGT‑001 / SGT‑002** | **18C** (U.S. Army Cyber Operations Officer) <br> **1B4X2** (Air Force Cyber Warfare Officer) | **Identify**, **Protect**, **Detect**, **Respond**, **Recover** | **Lead – Cyber Operations Lead**, **Analyze – Red Team**, **Educate – Cyber Educator** |
+| **WO‑001 / WO‑002** | **18A** (U.S. Army Cyber Operations Officer – Senior) <br> **1B4X3** (Air Force Cyber Warfare Senior Officer) | **All five CSF functions** (full‑cycle) | **Educate – Cyber Educator**, **Operate & Maintain – Cybersecurity Architect**, **Lead – Cyber Policy & Governance** |
+
+*Key observations*
+
+1. **Progressive CSF coverage** – DP 3 covers Identify/Protect/Detect, DP 4 adds Respond/Recover, DP 5 achieves full‑cycle coverage.
+2. **NICE alignment** – Early DPs map to *technical analyst* roles; later DPs map to *leadership, architecture, and policy* roles, mirroring the NICE career ladder.
+3. **U.S. MOS/AFSC parallels** give a common language for joint training and interoperability.
+
